  "context_pill": "Section 115BAC Tax Computation",
  "example_summary": "Computing tax liability for Mr. X with ₹ 16,00,000 income under the default regime for A.Y. 2026-27.",
  "source_provision": "### **Section 115BAC Concessional Tax Slab Rates**\n\n| Total Income Slab (₹) | Applicable Tax Rate (%) |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| Up to ₹ 4,00,000 | Nil |\n| ₹ 4,00,001 to ₹ 8,00,000 | 5% |\n| ₹ 8,00,001 to ₹ 12,00,000 | 10% |\n| ₹ 12,00,001 to ₹ 16,00,000 | 15% |\n| ₹ 16,00,001 to ₹ 20,00,000 | 20% |\n| ₹ 20,00,001 to ₹ 24,00,000 | 25% |\n| Above ₹ 24,00,000 | 30% |\n\n\n### **Statutory Conditions & Mechanism**\n\n* **Default Application**: Section 115BAC(1A) operates as the default tax regime for eligible assessees unless explicitly opted out.\n* **Statutory Surcharge & Cess**: Basic tax computed under slab rates is increased by applicable Surcharge and mandatory 4% Health and Education Cess.\n\n\n> [!IMPORTANT] Health and Education Cess Statutory Levy\n> Health and Education Cess at the rate of 4% is levied on the total basic income tax plus surcharge across all income slabs.",
